Architectural Principles (John)

Principle 1 – Reuse Before Create

* Reuse existing tables, APIs, and components wherever possible.
* If a new feature shares 70–80% of an existing model, extend the current implementation instead of creating new tables.

Principle 2 – Monorepo First

* Keep all applications aligned within the monorepo.
* Avoid duplicate functionality across applications.
* Build reusable components and shared business logic.

Principle 3 – AI-First Platform

* LangSmith → Observability
* LangGraph → AI orchestration
* Knowledge Base → Content management
* PDP/PEP → Authorization
* Human-in-the-loop approval before publishing AI-generated content.

